          </register>
          <register>
            <name>CFGRAM</name>
            <description>22nm Ram Control Register</description>
            <addressOffset>0x010</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x01000053</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMEMAA</name>
                <description>RAM port A  pins slow down memory access and provide extra time for memory read and write operations. The access time, cycle time, and margin increase as the pins are driven from 000-111, respectively. That is, 000 is the fastest setting and 111 the slowest</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>2</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMEMAB</name>
                <description>RAM port B  pins slow down memory access and provide extra time for memory read and write operations. The access time, cycle time, and margin increase as the pins are driven from 000-111, respectively. That is, 000 is the fastest setting and 111 the slowest</description>
                <lsb>4</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMEMASA</name>
                <description>RAM EMASA enables the bitline keeper. Set EMASA to 1 to enable the bitline keeper. The memory provides a bitline keeper for Port A read operations. The keeper affects the cycle time in the read cycle. It does not affect the access time. Enabling the bitline keeper can help to counteract the effects of leakage in a high-leakage process environment.</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>8</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMSTOV</name>
                <description>The RAM STOV feature allows you to override the self-timed generation of the clock pulse internal to the memory. When the STOV is asserted, the internal clock pulse is generated directly from the high phase of the external clock input.</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>12</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMWABLM</name>
                <description>RAM write assist setting. 0 for 0.8V. 1 for 0.7,0.6V</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>17</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>CFGRAMWABL</name>
                <description>When logic 1, enable write assist for RAMs</description>
                <lsb>24</lsb>
                <msb>24</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>CFGDUMMY</name>
            <description>Dummy Register</description>
            <addressOffset>0x014</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00C0FFEE</resetValue>
